{
  "title": "A curated kcal-only entry hides the density a learned estimate had",
  "description": "\"tonkatsu sauce\" was learned on prod as an estimate with grams_per_cup, so \"1 tbsp tonkatsu sauce\" counted at #825. \
A later commit added a curated entry with only a cited kcal_per_100g (USDA Branded 2455990); the curated entry now wins and the line is \"Missing density for this food\". \
Any curated entry added without a density can regress a learned name the same way. \
Fix: when the matched entry has no grams_per_cup, fall back to the learned estimate's grams_per_cup (and grams_per_piece) for the same name before the committed estimated weights, or require a density when a curated entry replaces a learned estimate (and cite one for tonkatsu sauce). \
Measure with make ingredient-prod-report. \
Server-side only (ramekin-core catalog/nutrition): no web or iOS change.",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 3,
  "type": "bug",
  "labels": [
    "catalog",
    "nutrition",
